# The provisioning scripts run on Linux. Never check them out with CRLF:
# bash fails on the trailing \r with errors that point nowhere useful.
*.sh                text eol=lf
# Installed into the distro as executables; extensionless, so *.sh misses them.
provision/bin/*     text eol=lf
# The runner runs inside the distro, and the plan is copied in verbatim. CRLF
# would break loop.py's shebang and would ride into every brief the solver reads.
*.py                text eol=lf
*.json              text eol=lf
plan/*.md           text eol=lf
*.md                text
# Host-side helpers run under cmd.exe / PowerShell 5.1, which needs CRLF and
# chokes on non-ASCII in a BOM-less file (see provision/README 3-6).
*.cmd               text eol=crlf
*.ps1               text eol=crlf
